  "relationships": [],
  "limitations": [
    "This collection holds only the Official Language Division circulars in the issuer's table with English titles (2010-2019): check points for the Official Language Policy (2010, 2011, 2012, 2019), the annual Hindi programme (2011, 2012), quarterly reports and inspection (2011-2012), bilingual website material (2010), standard letter head (2011), use of Hindi on computers (2012), simple language in Hindi translation (2012), the Rs. currency symbol (2013) and the 2015 arrangement for using Official Language Wing staff. Circulars with only Hindi titles (2010-2026), including the Hindi teaching scheme, incentive schemes, awards and later check-point circulars, are not included because they cannot be classified from the issuer table without Hindi OCR.",
    "Most circulars are in Hindi first and are OCR'd with an English model, so the Hindi text is unreliable; the English portions (subject lines, names, dates in Roman figures) were checked, but the Hindi directions should be read from the page image. Their headers show no legible date, so issue dates follow the issuer listing and were not checked against the letter.",
    "No circular here states that an earlier check-points circular is withdrawn; each reissue is a separate dated circular and no supersession is asserted. Whether the 2019 check points are still in force is not recorded here.",
    "Hindi fortnight, Hindi conferences, departmental magazines, workshops, training and awards circulars (routine or promotional) are deliberately left out; they are listed under the Official Language catalog rows as routine or communication.",
    "No commencement dates are recorded; the circulars state none beyond their issue date in the English passages read.",
    "PDFs were read from the issuer mirror on 4 November 2026 because the public site returned 404 for these paths; recorded SHA-256 values apply to those files. Scanned pages are OCR. Issue dates were checked against the document headers."
  ]
}
